 <LayoutItem labelText="BDAs are designed to be permeable, channel-spanning structures with a constant crest elevation, constructed with a mixture of woody debris and fill material to form a pond and mimic a natural beaver dam. BDAs will generally be used within structure complexes located in primary and secondary channels and floodplain surfaces where they can increase the duration of floodplain inundation, and horizontally disperse flow." visibility="1" htmlState="0" frame="false" marginY="0" zValue="44" id="" opacity="1" size="10.6412,1.80588,in" type="65641" templateUuid="{1e0e2a74-a83a-4316-9889-0864b8622b49}" halign="1" referencePoint="0" outlineWidthM="0.3,mm" marginX="2" frameJoinStyle="miter" itemRotation="0" valign="32" uuid="{1e0e2a74-a83a-4316-9889-0864b8622b49}" position="13.2606,8.20011,in" blendMode="0" positionOnPage="13.2606,8.20011,in" excludeFromExports="0" groupUuid="" background="false" positionLock="true">
